{"number":217,"state":"open","dependency":{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"mcp"},"manifest_path":"python/uv.lock","version_requirement":"= 1.28.1","scope":"runtime","relationship":"transitive"},"security_advisory":{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-84m7-p3x7-pcfv","cve_id":"CVE-2026-59951","summary":"MCP Python SDK: Unbounded Session Accumulation in StreamableHTTP Transport Enables Resource Exhaustion","description":"### Summary\nIn affected versions, a Streamable HTTP server in stateful mode (the default) never reclaimed session state:\n\n- sessions did not expire;\n- a client `DELETE` ended the session but left its entry registered;\n- a session whose first request was refused stayed registered with a running task.\n\nEach session also kept its parsed `initialize` parameters, and the number of sessions was unlimited. A client that could reach the endpoint could grow server memory without bound using ordinary short requests; only a restart reclaimed it.\n\n### Am I affected?\nYes, if you serve MCP over Streamable HTTP in stateful mode and clients you do not fully trust can reach the endpoint. Stateful mode is the default for:\n\n- `FastMCP` (1.x)\n- `MCPServer` and `Server.streamable_http_app()` (2.x)\n- `StreamableHTTPSessionManager`\n\nAffected versions: 1.8.0 through 1.29.1, and 2.0.0 through 2.1.1.\n\nNot affected:\n\n- servers on 1.12.0 or later passing `stateless_http=True` (no sessions are kept)\n- servers using only the stdio or SSE transports\n\nAuthentication limits who can open sessions, not how many a token holder can open.\n\n### Fix\nUpgrade to `mcp` 1.30.0 (1.x) or 2.2.0 (2.x) or later. In those versions:\n\n- a session with no request in flight for `session_idle_timeout` seconds (default 1800) is closed and its ID then answers `404`; open streams and in-progress requests keep it alive;\n- at most `max_sessions` sessions exist at once (default 10000); a request that would open another is answered `503`;\n- a session is discarded as soon as it ends, whether by `DELETE`, expiry, or a refused opening request.\n\nBoth settings are keyword arguments on `FastMCP(...)` (1.x), `MCPServer.run()` / `streamable_http_app()` (2.x) and `StreamableHTTPSessionManager`; `None` disables them.\n\nThis bounds retention rather than eliminating it: a live session still holds its `initialize` parameters (up to roughly twice the 4 MiB body limit), and an `initialize` with invalid parameters still opens a session that expires like any other. On a small host, lower `session_idle_timeout`, `max_sessions` and `max_request_body_size` to fit.\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, pass `stateless_http=True` (1.12.0 or later) where you need no per-session state, or restrict who can reach the endpoint.","severity":"medium","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-84m7-p3x7-pcfv","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-59951","type":"CVE"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-84m7-p3x7-pcfv"},{"url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-59951"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3395"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/pull/3426"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/92120b4b0f50385af096592d7cee932fc1d994e7"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/commit/d2290ca3434731b68ea3e2270bc06a6e6575931b"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/releases/tag/v1.30.0"},{"url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/releases/tag/v2.2.0"},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-84m7-p3x7-pcfv"}],"published_at":"2026-10-15T20:13:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T20:13:14Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"mcp"},"severity":"medium","vulnerable_version_range":">= 1.8.0, < 1.30.0","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"1.30.0"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"mcp"},"severity":"medium","vulnerable_version_range":">= 2.0.0, < 2.2.0","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"2.2.0"}}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":6.9}},"epss":{"percentage":0.00458,"percentile":0.38172},"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":7.5},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-400","name":"Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-770","name":"Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-772","name":"Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime"}],"classification":"general"},"security_vulnerability":{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"mcp"},"severity":"medium","vulnerable_version_range":">= 1.8.0, < 1.30.0","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"1.30.0"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KooshaPari/AgilePlus/dependabot/alerts/217","html_url":"https://github.com/KooshaPari/AgilePlus/security/dependabot/217","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:22:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T22:22:23Z","dismissal_request":null,"assignees":[],"dismissed_at":null,"dismissed_by":null,"dismissed_reason":null,"dismissed_comment":null,"fixed_at":null,"auto_dismissed_at":null}=== alerts 215, 216, 214 details ===
